-- Deep Cut Theatre — a second pass of verified films, bringing the ten
-- channels from migration 0009 up toward the density of the original four.
-- Same bar as every prior batch: hosted on the filmmaker's (or the actual
-- producing outlet's) own official Vimeo/YouTube account, confirmed via the
-- platform's own oEmbed response rather than a search snippet, and a
-- pedigree line stating the exact award and year.
--
-- Two judgment calls worth recording. Off the Rails' "Kung Fury" and
-- Tomorrow's Problem's dropped "Rakka" both came back with real, verified
-- hosting but no festival selection at all — direct-to-YouTube releases
-- rather than festival films. Kung Fury did screen at Cannes (Directors'
-- Fortnight, an official sidebar, no award), which is enough of a pedigree
-- line to state precisely; Rakka had nothing to state at all and isn't here.
-- Overtime's "Slomo" and "A Swim Lesson" are genuinely great, real
-- award-carrying films whose sport-ness is a stretch — a rollerblader and a
-- swim instructor, not a game with a score — included on the same logic as
-- "Curfew" in Wrong Turn: a strong film that leans into the channel's mood
-- more than its literal subject.

